2024\/01\/codepen-300x150.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/codepen-768x384.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/codepen.io\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">CodePen<\/a>&nbsp;is among the top&nbsp;tools for frontend developers&nbsp;as it is intuitive and easy to use. It offers multiple functionalities to design&nbsp;frontend&nbsp;web pages. As it offers all the essential features of an Integrated Development environment in a web browser, developers use it to build an entire project.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Professional developers can also use this tool to make the development process hassle-free. It is meant for&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/front-end-development-projects\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">frontend&nbsp;projects<\/a>, so if you want to design client-side elements,&nbsp;CodePen&nbsp;should be your go-to solution. This online code editor supports HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of&nbsp;CodePen&nbsp;Web Dev Tool<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Open-source SAAS instrument.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Completely free, so you can start using it without a second thought.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offers internal learning resources.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Has an intuitive and simple interface.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">10. Grunt<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"291\" height=\"343\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/grunt.webp\" alt=\"Grunt\" class=\"wp-image-21470\" style=\"width:201px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/grunt.webp 291w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/grunt-255x300.webp 255w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 291px) 100vw, 291px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/gruntjs.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Grunt<\/a> is a popular JavaScript task runner used to automate repetitive web development tasks, such as minification, unit testing, linting, and compilation. You just&nbsp;have to&nbsp;install and configure the task using a Grunt file, and your tasks will be easy. It is a flexible and widely adopted web development tool used by developers to complete a project efficiently within the stipulated time.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Grunt is known for its ever-growing repository of plugins, which creates a great coding environment for developers. They use Grunt to implement coding style guides throughout the code base of a project, which adds readability and consistency to the code. Also, it offers image optimization and linting capabilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It is a free and easy-to-use tool that you can download from its official website, through NPM, or any NodeJS\/Javascript&nbsp;Package Manager. It is released under the MIT license and is available for free on GitHub. There are several plugins too that you can use or create your own plugins.&nbsp;Vite&nbsp;has&nbsp;largely replaced&nbsp;task runners like Grunt and Gulp for new projects.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Grunt Web Development Tool<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Needs a single command to carry out different tasks automatically.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Developers can add and publish Grunt plugins on NPM.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Developers can create, extend, and change tasks according to their requirements. Each task has&nbsp;distinct&nbsp;configurable settings.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>As the project expands and more codebases are added, Grunt helps manage complex development processes.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Allows access to an array of plugins to perform JavaScript tasks on static content.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">11. Envato<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"315\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/envato.webp\" alt=\"Envato\" class=\"wp-image-6053\" style=\"width:306px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/envato.webp 600w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/envato-300x158.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/elements.envato.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Envato<\/a>&nbsp;is typically a&nbsp;frontend&nbsp;development tool with a great collection of built-in HTML5 templates for developers to design user interfaces. It supports almost all&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/best-programming-languages\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">popular programming languages<\/a>, including HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, along with a number of web application frameworks, hence offering templates for Bootstrap, Laravel,&nbsp;VueJS, and Angular.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Its collection of 1000+ readymade HTML5 templates makes it a go-to choice among developers who use it to&nbsp;optimize&nbsp;CSS and JavaScript coding techniques.&nbsp;Thus&nbsp;saving ample coding time and enhancing page speed scores.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of&nbsp;Envato&nbsp;Web Design Tool<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Several built-in features for front-end developers.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Thousands of HTML5 templates.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Supports most programming languages.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">12. Postman<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1280\" height=\"645\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/postman.webp\" alt=\"Postman\" class=\"wp-image-6062\" style=\"width:370px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/postman.webp 1280w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/postman-300x151.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/postman-1024x516.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/postman-768x387.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.postman.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Postman<\/a>&nbsp;was initially a Google Chrome extension that has now marked its place among the top application programming interface (API) testing tools. It opens an easier way for developers to work with APIs, including building, testing, sharing, and&nbsp;modifying&nbsp;APIs. There are built-in features that developers can use to&nbsp;monitor, debug, and run requests, along with shared workspaces for improved collaboration.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Postman&nbsp;is known for its user-friendly interface for inspecting responses, sending HTTP requests, and testing API endpoints. Using these features, the tool streamlines the web development workflow and&nbsp;maintains&nbsp;API reliability.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are looking for free&nbsp;web programmer tools, you can try its free version with basic functionality. However, for advanced features, choose from the three paid plans. The basic plan costs $12\/month per user with a 30-day collection recovery and a single custom domain.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Free is single-user, Solo is $9, Team is $19, Enterprise is $49 per user\/month, plus a verify-before-publish note.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Its Newman feature allows users to integrate APIs with popular code deployment pipeline tools, including Jenkins, Bamboo, and TeamCity. Also, users can upload files and create custom reports using this feature.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Collaboration features, such as commenting, workspace, and team discovery, improve team collaboration.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Using API documentation tools, developers can automatically create professional API documents shared publicly or exclusively with team members.&nbsp;Customers can use this proper documentation to integrate API.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>You can visualize API data using reports, which include documentation, testing, and monitoring.&nbsp;These reports enable users to check the performance and service-level agreement (SLA) compliance.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>API governance allows developers to find any security glitches or inconsistencies during API design and testing. Hence, they can create more secure and top-quality web applications.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Users can navigate the interface, manage APIs, and see the tasks of other team members in the workspace.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">13. Sketch<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"650\" height=\"326\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/sketch.webp\" alt=\"Sketch\" class=\"wp-image-21471\" style=\"width:422px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/sketch.webp 650w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/sketch-300x150.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.sketch.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Sketch<\/a> is one of the best&nbsp;website development apps&nbsp;for macOS used for designing pixel-perfect graphics. It comes with a robust vector-based design toolkit to simplify the development of&nbsp;different types&nbsp;of prototypes and interfaces. It allows constant resizing and more, offering a one-stop solution for all your design needs.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This tool also&nbsp;possesses&nbsp;the ability to export code and presets and integrate with&nbsp;numerous&nbsp;plugins, non-destructive vector editing, and collaborative tools. There are&nbsp;3&nbsp;paid plans. Standard&nbsp;is&nbsp;$12\/editor\/month, Business&nbsp;is&nbsp;$20\/editor\/month, Mac-only license&nbsp;is&nbsp;$120\/year.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>They offer unlimited free viewers, and developers can use them to assess the design. There is a&nbsp;Business&nbsp;plan as well for 25+ editors. You can opt for a 30-day free trial to try Sketch before buying a premium plan.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Developers and designers can work together on a single project in real time.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Using the handoff feature, developers can copy design style values and export assets.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>There are various third-party plugins and integrations that improve its functionality and workflow.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Allows users to import data from text files into mockups.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Creating mockups is simple due to drag-and-drop features, such as Smart Guides for&nbsp;accurate&nbsp;alignment and Sketch Symbols for designing reusable design components.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">14. Docker<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"960\" height=\"794\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/docker.webp\" alt=\"Docker\" class=\"wp-image-17027\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1.209127638991635;width:304px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/docker.webp 960w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/docker-300x248.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/docker-768x635.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.docker.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Docker<\/a> is used to deploy applications in virtual containers. It is a free tool that enables developers to deploy and scale apps quickly across multiple environments by combining the source code of an app and the libraries&nbsp;required&nbsp;to run it. This&nbsp;cuts down&nbsp;the time&nbsp;required&nbsp;to install the code and dependencies separately.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The tools can be used for free with unlimited public repositories. There are three paid plans, too&nbsp;&#8211; Pro&nbsp;is for $9\/mo, Team is for $15\/user\/mo, &amp; Business is for&nbsp;$24\/user\/mo. Moreover, companies with 250+ employees or $10M+ revenue must pay.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Dockers is known for its portability, which allows users to build and install complex web applications on a machine and evaluate their performance.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>It offers an automated container builder, container versioning, and reusable container templates, along with an open-source repository of user-made containers.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Using Docker containers and&nbsp;cron&nbsp;jobs, users can automate their tasks. They can also save ample time by avoiding repetitive tasks.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>It has a wide community, regular contributors, and a dedicated Slack channel.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-7ab0c851046a906928eb9cd2d144f8f2\"><strong>Read More Web Development Related Guides<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-web-development\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">What is Web Development<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Web Development Project Ideas<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-careers\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Careers in Web Development<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-does-web-developer-do\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">What Does Web Developer Do<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Web Development Frameworks<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-future\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Web Development Future<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-languages\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Web Development Languages<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-developer-job-description\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Web Developer Job Description<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">How to Become Web Developer<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/is-web-development-good-career\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Is Web Development Good Career<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-books\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Web Development Books<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/types-of-web-development\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Types of Web Development<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-learn-web-development\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">How to Learn Web Development<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-roadmap\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Web Development Roadmap<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">15. Angular<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"600\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/angular.webp\" alt=\"Angular\" class=\"wp-image-9173\" style=\"width:364px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/angular.webp 1200w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/angular-300x150.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/angular-1024x512.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/angular-768x384.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/angular-150x75.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/angular.dev\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Angular<\/a> is one of the best&nbsp;tools for&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/front-end-development\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">front-end development<\/a><strong>&nbsp;<\/strong>introduced by Google. It can work with <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/backend-technologies\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">backend technologies<\/a> and combines user&nbsp;interface&nbsp;and business logic. It is used to create an array of apps, such as&nbsp;progressive web applications&nbsp;(PWA), single-page applications (SPA), and large enterprise apps. As you will use this cross-platform solution, you will realize&nbsp;it\u2019s&nbsp;not only versatile but also offers amazing improvements and functions.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Angular is written in Typescript, which helps developers&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;consistency and write cleaner code. It offers ample UI components for web designers that speed up the web app development process. Also, developers can initialize, build, and scaffold Angular apps directly from the command line because of its ease of use. Moreover, with its two-way data binding function, one can change the app data using UI.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>It supports progressive web applications, which means Angular web apps are compatible with Android and iOS devices.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>With custom directives, users can improve HTML and CSS capabilities to build dynamic web apps.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Two-way data binding allows singular behavior for the app. Hence, it reduces the risk of errors.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Dependency injection (DI) is a feature used to split an app into a group of components that can be injected into one another as dependencies.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Due to various well-organized modules, conducting unit testing is hassle-free.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>RxJS&nbsp;is an effective way to share data while reducing the number of resources&nbsp;required&nbsp;for the purpose.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Its powerful CLI makes the job easier for developers with its set of coding tools. There are third-party libraries, too, to address complex issues.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">16. jQuery<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"225\" height=\"225\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/jquery.webp\" alt=\"JQuery\" class=\"wp-image-5285\" style=\"width:211px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/jquery.webp 225w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/jquery-150x150.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 225px) 100vw, 225px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/jquery.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">jQuery<\/a> needs no introduction. This lightweight <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/best-javascript-frameworks\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">JavaScript library<\/a> is an essential\u00a0component\u00a0to simplify HTML document manipulation, animation, and event handling. It was introduced in 2005 to overcome common issues faced by JavaScript, such as unapproachable syntax, browser inconsistency, and a few other complex aspects, which make JS less functional. jQuery is a cross-platform solution that makes the frontend development process easier.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It has a concise syntax, which lets developers build more interactive and dynamic web pages. Also, its extensive plugin ecosystem enhances its capabilities and allows users to add&nbsp;cutting-edge&nbsp;features to their projects without writing lengthy code.&nbsp;jQuery&nbsp;offers a wider scope for navigation documents and animation while addressing issues of JS.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-15e48e0c4b97cd13d8787f9f94ad76d7\"><em><strong>Note:&nbsp;<\/strong>It&#8217;s&nbsp;now a legacy tool; new projects use React\/Vue\/Svelte.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of jQuery<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Offers a wide range of event-handling methods.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Makes DOM traversal and manipulation easier.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Includes cross-browser compatibility and consistent behavior.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">17. Kubernetes<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"569\" height=\"310\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/kubernetes.webp\" alt=\"Kubernetes\" class=\"wp-image-17028\" style=\"width:311px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/kubernetes.webp 569w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/kubernetes-300x163.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 569px) 100vw, 569px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/kubernetes.io\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Kubernetes<\/a> is another open-source container orchestration platform used for deploying, scaling, and managing modern web applications. The tool is adept at organizing application containers into logical units to ensure easy discovery and management. Using its features, developers can deliver applications regularly and transfer workloads. With consistent app monitoring and deployment, it avoids a total outage.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Kubernetes<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Mounts the selected storage system to enhance user experiences and reduce latency.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The tool can run across different infrastructures, which include&nbsp;on-premise&nbsp;data centers and private\/public\/ and hybrid cloud.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improves application performance through regular monitoring and replacing any unhealthy containers.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Kubernetes Secrets stores critical data, including SSH keys, authentication tokens, and passwords.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Users can build and update secrets without rebuilding container images or exposing them to stack configuration.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>It assesses applications to mitigate the chances of any potential errors or issues.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Scales each container automatically based on custom metrics and resources available.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Exposes containers to their IP addresses and DNS names and enables load balancing during high traffic to ensure stability.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">18. Gulp<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"228\" height=\"510\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/gulp.webp\" alt=\"Gulp\" class=\"wp-image-21472\" style=\"width:96px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/gulp.webp 228w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/gulp-134x300.webp 134w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 228px) 100vw, 228px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/gulpjs.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Gulp<\/a> is a popular JavaScript-based tool that streamlines and automates the development process. This is one of the commonly used&nbsp;tools to develop&nbsp;website&nbsp;that&nbsp;performs&nbsp;various tasks. It also handles resources that are a part of a larger set of instructions.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Gulp<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Way more flexible&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Faster due to streams.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-e168beef2a54ae1ff198c9b96b7b1d8a\"><em><strong>Note:<\/strong>&nbsp;It&#8217;s&nbsp;used less for new projects now (Vite has taken over).<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">19. ReactJS<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"464\" height=\"528\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/reactjs.webp\" alt=\"React Js\" class=\"wp-image-5217\" style=\"width:200px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/reactjs.webp 464w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/reactjs-264x300.webp 264w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 464px) 100vw, 464px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/react.dev\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">React<\/a> is an open-source JS library used to create reusable and modern UI components. It is an adaptable, declarative, and effective library that allows users to write and pre-build components easily. This speeds up the development process and makes it more efficient. This frontend framework takes care of the view layer of an application.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Moreover, it is used for server&nbsp;rendering&nbsp;with NodeJS and power mobile apps with React Native.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of ReactJS Web Development Tool<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Virtual Document Object Model (DOM) is used to arrange XHTML, HTML, or XML-based documents into a proper structure, which is more acceptable to browsers while parsing through elements of a web app.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Its rendering feature reduces the page load time, which boosts website ranking on&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/serp\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SERPs<\/a>.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The components of React have their own logic and control, making it easier to track the code for complex tasks.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>You can switch between versions easily.&nbsp;Meta&#8217;s &#8216;code mods\u2019&nbsp;automate most of the process.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The user-side data can be simultaneously represented on the server side as well, making it a lightweight tool.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Due to its one-way data binding, troubleshooting is much hassle-free in React.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">20. Webpack<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"360\" height=\"140\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/webpack.webp\" alt=\"WebPack\" class=\"wp-image-6059\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/webpack.webp 360w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/webpack-300x117.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/webpack.js.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Webpack<\/a>, one of the well-known&nbsp;web programming tools, is a module generator for web applications. It&nbsp;comprehends&nbsp;JavaScript and JSON and&nbsp;optimizes&nbsp;CSS, JS, and other assets. This improves website performance and page loading speed.&nbsp;It follows a modular approach and supports code splitting, which enables efficient management of dependencies.&nbsp;Therefore, it is a crucial web development tool for better workflow.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Also, it uses a loader to transform frontend files, such as CSS and HTML, into modules, which provides users with a comprehensive solution.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Webpack<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Comes with an extensive plugin ecosystem and configuration options.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Bundles and&nbsp;optimizes&nbsp;assets to enable faster loading.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Output tells Webpack about the location and structure of the created bundles.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Plugins offer several features, such as minifying, printing, etc.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Supports code splitting and lazy loading, which enhances performance.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">21. Tailwind CSS<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"738\" height=\"369\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/tailwind-css.webp\" alt=\"Tailwind CSS\" class=\"wp-image-21473\" style=\"width:350px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/tailwind-css.webp 738w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/tailwind-css-300x150.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 738px) 100vw, 738px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/tailwindcss.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Tailwind CSS<\/a> is a utility-first CSS framework that has become one of the most popular tools for web development styling in 2026. Instead of writing custom CSS files, developers compose designs directly in their markup using utility classes, which keeps styling fast, consistent, and easy to&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;across a project. It pairs especially well with modern frameworks like React and Next.js.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-5b7e271448582f3dc6b27c47cabe6be0\"><strong>Explore Our Web Development Related Courses<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/full-stack-developer-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Online Full Stack Developer Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/wordpress-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Online WordPress Course<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Tailwind CSS<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Utility-first classes let you style elements directly in your markup without leaving your HTML.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Highly customizable through a single configuration file for colors, spacing, and breakpoints.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Produces small, optimized CSS by removing unused styles in production.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Free and&nbsp;open-source, with a large community and ecosystem of components.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">22. Next.js<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"471\" height=\"424\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/next-js.webp\" alt=\"Next.JS\" class=\"wp-image-21474\" style=\"width:231px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/next-js.webp 471w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/next-js-300x270.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 471px) 100vw, 471px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/nextjs.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Next.js<\/a> is the leading&nbsp;full-stack&nbsp;React framework and one of the top web development tools for building production web apps. It adds server-side rendering, static site generation, routing, and API routes on top of React. It is the standard choice when you want&nbsp;React&nbsp;with full-stack capabilities and excellent performance, and it deploys seamlessly to&nbsp;Vercel.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Next.js<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Supports server-side&nbsp;rendering&nbsp;and static generation for faster load times and better SEO.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Built-in file-based routing and API routes for <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-full-stack-development\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">full-stack development<\/a>.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Image optimization and performance features out of the box.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong integration with the&nbsp;Vercel&nbsp;hosting platform.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">23. Vite<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"410\" height=\"403\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/vite.webp\" alt=\"Vite\" class=\"wp-image-21475\" style=\"width:226px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/vite.webp 410w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/vite-300x295.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 410px) 100vw, 410px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/vite.dev\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Vite<\/a> has become the default build tool for new frontend projects, offering near-instant dev server startup and&nbsp;fast hot&nbsp;module replacement. It is built on native ES modules and an&nbsp;esbuild-based pipeline, and it has&nbsp;largely replaced&nbsp;older bundlers and task runners for new work.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Vite<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Extremely fast development server startup and hot module replacement.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Optimized production builds with code splitting.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Works with React, Vue, Svelte, and other frameworks.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Free and&nbsp;open-source&nbsp;with a growing plugin ecosystem.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">24. Figma<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"700\" height=\"418\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/figma.webp\" alt=\"Figma\" class=\"wp-image-19803\" style=\"width:348px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/figma.webp 700w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/figma-300x179.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.figma.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Figma<\/a> is the market-leading collaborative design tool for UI\/UX and an essential part of the modern web development toolkit. Developers and designers can design and prototype interfaces directly in the browser with real-time multiplayer editing. Its developer handoff features let engineers inspect designs, copy values, and export assets, making it the standard bridge between design and development.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Figma<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Browser-based design with real-time collaboration for multiple users.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reusable components and design systems for consistency across projects.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Developer handoff with inspectable design values and exportable assets.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Free tier available, with paid plans for teams and organizations.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">25. Playwright<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"225\" height=\"225\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/playwright.webp\" alt=\"Playwright\" class=\"wp-image-21476\" style=\"width:261px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/playwright.webp 225w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/playwright-150x150.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 225px) 100vw, 225px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/playwright.dev\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Playwright<\/a> is a fast, reliable end-to-end testing framework that automates real browsers across Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. It has become a go-to choice for testing in 2026, valued for its stability, cross-browser coverage, and strong integration with CI\/CD pipelines.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Playwright<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Automates testing across Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit browsers.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reliable, less flaky tests compared to older UI testing tools.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Works well in CI\/CD pipelines for automated test runs.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Free and&nbsp;open-source.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">26. Vercel&nbsp;and Netlify<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1668\" height=\"943\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/vercel-netlify.webp\" alt=\"Vercel\u00a0and Netlify\" class=\"wp-image-21477\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1.7688283486329088;width:374px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/vercel-netlify.webp 1668w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/vercel-netlify-300x170.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/vercel-netlify-1024x579.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/vercel-netlify-768x434.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/vercel-netlify-1536x868.webp 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1668px) 100vw, 1668px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/vercel.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Vercel<\/a>&nbsp;and <a href=\"https:\/\/www.netlify.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Netlify<\/a> are popular hosting and deployment platforms for modern web applications. Both offer Git-based continuous deployment, global content delivery, and preview environments for every change, making it easy to ship and scale frontend apps.&nbsp;Vercel&nbsp;is&nbsp;optimized&nbsp;for Next.js, while Netlify is a strong choice for static sites and&nbsp;Jamstack&nbsp;apps.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of&nbsp;Vercel&nbsp;and Netlify<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Git-based continuous deployment that ships&nbsp;changes&nbsp;automatically.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Global edge delivery for fast load times worldwide.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Preview deployments for every pull request.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Free tiers available, with paid plans for teams and higher usage.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">AI-Powered Web Development Tools<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The biggest change to the list of tools for web development in recent years is the rise of <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-artificial-intelligence\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">AI<\/a>. Most professional developers now use one or more AI coding tools every day, and any list of the top web development tools in 2026&nbsp;has to&nbsp;start here. These tools split into two groups: assistants that help you write code while you stay in control, and app builders that generate working applications from a prompt.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. GitHub Copilot<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"422\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/github-copilot.webp\" alt=\"GitHub Copilot\" class=\"wp-image-21478\" style=\"width:358px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/github-copilot.webp 800w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/github-copilot-300x158.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/github-copilot-768x405.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/github.com\/features\/copilot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">GitHub Copilot<\/a> is the most widely adopted AI coding assistant in the world. It is integrated into Visual Studio Code, JetBrains,&nbsp;Neovim, and the GitHub platform itself. Copilot has evolved from a simple autocomplete tool into a broader assistant that can explain code, generate tests, review pull requests, and&nbsp;assist&nbsp;across the entire project lifecycle. Its broad editor support and low adoption friction make it the safest choice for teams that already work on GitHub.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of GitHub Copilot<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Suggests code completions, whole functions, and unit tests based on your coding context.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Works across most popular editors, including VS Code, JetBrains, and&nbsp;Neovim.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Can explain unfamiliar code, generate tests, and help review pull requests.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offers a free tier with monthly limits, with Pro plans around $10\/month and Business plans around $19\/user\/month.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Cursor<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"547\" height=\"365\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/cursor.webp\" alt=\"Cursor\" class=\"wp-image-21479\" style=\"width:341px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/cursor.webp 547w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/cursor-300x200.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 547px) 100vw, 547px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/cursor.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Cursor<\/a> is an AI-native code editor built as a fork of Visual Studio Code, with AI baked into every layer rather than added as a plugin. Its standout feature is multi-file editing (known as Composer) along with codebase-wide context indexing, which grounds suggestions in your actual repository instead of generic patterns. It is widely considered the benchmark AI IDE for professional developers in 2026.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Features of Cursor<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Multi-file editing lets developers refactor across an entire project in one step.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Codebase indexing grounds AI suggestions in your real repository.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Supports multiple underlying AI models for different tasks.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Free tier available, with Pro plans starting around $20\/user\/month.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-402fd4ad0bf7f321de8c8b3f3edae4fb\"><strong>Read More on Topics Related to Web Development<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/best-programming-languages\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Best Programming Languages<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/backend-languages\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Backend Programming Languages<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/html-vs-html5\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">HTML vs HTML5<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/will-ai-replace-full-stack-developers\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Will AI Replace Developers<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/html-projects\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">HTML Project Ideas<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/programming-languages-types\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Programming Languages Types<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/front-end-technologies\/\